      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To investigate the immunoregulation of dendritic cells in allergic rhinitis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHOD",
          "content": "Adopting the cell culture and the enzyme linked immunosorbant assay to examine the patients' Th1/Th2 in the blood. Observing that how is the DC's function in immunoregulation of allergic rhinitis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULT",
          "content": "The concentration of the IFN-gamma advanced obviously in post-stimulatory supernatant liquid after using the mature DC."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The mature dendritic cells can polarize naive T-cells into Th1 effector cells, and are recognized as having a central role in the establishment of T-cell memory and peripheral immune tolerance. DC could be exploited as targets for therapy in asthma and allergic rhinitis."
        }
      ]},
